  "pieces_total": 47,
  "rationale": "Hand-chosen convex hulls of the load-bearing printed parts, one per phalanx, plus a separate hull per silicone pad (fingertip skin, proximal/middle pads, palm/hypothenar/thenar pads) in class v21_pad: the pads are the real contact surfaces and get rubber friction, and a pad hull sticks out of the phalanx hull on the palm side, so grasps touch pads first. CoACD only where one hull would be badly wrong: the palm shell (thumb bay cut) and the wrist ring (a loop). Hulls reduced to <= 64 vertices by greedy farthest-outside insertion (deviation listed per piece, inside the true hull). Few small convex pieces keep GPU (MJX/Warp) narrow-phase cost low; the forearm is 2 coarse hulls (it only meets the table)."
 },
